<bold>BMI [kgm-</bold>
<sup>
<bold>2</bold>
</sup>
<bold>]</bold>
</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22.1 &#x000b1; 3.21</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">21.4 &#x000b1; 3.21</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">22.7 &#x000b1; 3.21</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">p = 0.123</td></tr></tbody></table></alternatives><table-wrap-foot><fn id="t001fn001"><p>X&#x02013;mean, SD&#x02013;standard deviation.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><p>The values of displacement (Dm) describing muscle stiffness presented in the study, obtained using tensiomyographic method are mean values of measurements performed on the left and right side of the body.</p><p>In the studied group the values of pelvic tilt measurements ranged from 10 to 26 degrees (X = 16.9, SD = 5.34). The results of tensiomyographic analysis of the studied muscles are presented in <xref rid="pone.0312480.t002" ref-type="table">Table 2</xref>.</p><table-wrap position="float" id="pone.0312480.t002"><object-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1371/journal.pone.0312480.t002</object-id><label>Table 2</label><caption><title>Values of median (M), interquartile range (IQ) and the results of the analysis performed using the Kruskal-Wallis test for maximal muscle displacement (Dm) in groups formed based on the value of pelvic tilt.</title></caption><alternatives><graphic xlink:href="pone.0312480.t002" id="pone.0312480.t002g" position="float"/><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><colgroup span="1"><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/><col align="left" valign="middle" span="1"/></colgroup><thead><tr><th align="center" colspan="5" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1">Dm [mm]</th></tr><tr><th align="center" rowspan="2" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" colspan="1">Group<break/>Muscle</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Whole group</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Decreased pelvic tilt</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Normal<break/>pelvic tilt</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Increased<break/>pelvic tilt</th></tr><tr><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M<break/>IQ</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M<break/>IQ</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M<break/>IQ</th><th align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">M<break/>IQ</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="center" style="background-color:#FFFFFF" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
